It answers:
- 'the leak under plan reads as a dash, an underline or a typo' (all eight lenses): the leak is deleted and the light falls as an edgeless pool;
- 'placard jargon' and '12px brass placards too faint' (interaction, usability, type, skeptic): there is one plain-word placard per window at 13px;
- 'violet-edged starter keys are off-period' and 'blue-steel notches lean navy' (feedback, skeptic): there is one steel edge, with destinations in brass;
- 'starters feel like generic tabs' (style): they are engraved flush to the box's foot;
- 'green share still high' (soul, system, the designer): the slot bloom is cut and only Next is at full strength;
- 'Next up's empty lower half; the radar crowds a long location' (soul, interaction, usability): there is a fixed text column and a facts block, with the radar kept to its own track;
- 'the month view is plain' (style, system, skeptic, soul): it has lit numeral windows, tick-coloured chips and a dash per plan;
- 'the lists are the same generic rows' and 'the plate's lines do not reach the lists' (feedback): channels carry each cut's light to its rows;
- 'full-width Send on the phone is as loud as the title' (system): Send goes back in the From row;
- 'Ideas hides For and Status' (usability): they are visible selects;
- 'the odd full-width Sign-in group' (system): Sign-in is back in the column flow;
- 'the spend needle rests at zero in stills' (main lessons' open problem): the ghost needle and the limit tick fill it.

It avoids the crossing lessons' warnings in three ways:
- No ring-as-tick and no ring stops: the nodes are square.
- It does not paste a source's look: each graft is rebuilt as a cut, channel or round window in slate.
- It does not converge on the shared title or the field's ring setup strip, since setup keeps the line's full sentences.

It gives up:
- the stencil leak;
- the 'RINGS 1·2·4 WK' and '1 WK/DIV' placards;
- the bar-style spend meter in the left window;
- the cyan chip bars on the month;
- the violet, ochre and cyan starter notches;
- the Ideas filter disclosure.
